---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import LtvCacCalculator from '../../components/LtvCacCalculator.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="LTV:CAC Calculator" description="Calculate customer lifetime value, customer acquisition cost, and the LTV:CAC ratio investors look at.">
  <LtvCacCalculator client:load slot="tool" />
  <h2>Why the 3:1 rule of thumb exists</h2>
  <p>A common benchmark is that LTV should be at least 3x CAC — high enough to cover acquisition cost, support, and still leave healthy margin. Below 1:1 means you're losing money on every customer acquired.</p>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Treating 3:1 as a universal target</strong> regardless of industry or business model — the "right" ratio varies by margin structure and growth stage.</li>
    <li><strong>Calculating LTV and CAC over mismatched time periods</strong>, comparing numbers that aren't actually apples-to-apples.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Evaluating whether current acquisition spend is sustainable long-term</li>
    <li>Reporting unit economics health to investors or leadership</li>
    <li>Comparing LTV:CAC across different marketing channels</li>
  </ul>
</ToolLayout>
